<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexios II of Trebizond</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1282–1330</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexios II was Emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trabzon">Trebizond</a> from 1297 to 1330, the son of John II and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eudokia-palaiologina">Eudokia Palaiologina</a>. His long reign was a time of prosperity, when Trebizond flourished as a terminus of the trade route from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a> under Ilkhanid overlordship, with Genoese and Venetian merchants active in the city. He resisted Genoese pressure and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> raids, and his death was followed by years of civil war.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alexios-ii-of-trebizond.jpg" alt="Alexios II of Trebizond" width="320" height="293" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG Coins · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alexios_II_of_Trebizond.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
